    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is anchored today by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who represent our primary avenues for production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Brandon Young (4.78 xERA) and significant park factors, resulting in an elite efficiency score that makes him a must-start. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** faces Trey Yesavage, but his aggressive scoring is fueled by an exceptional park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage that outweighs the SP\u2019s moderate skill set. We are also high on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.88), who is poised to exploit a positive park environment and a favorable platoon matchup against Michael King, making him the most reliable middle-infield option in our daily rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today\u2019s lineup was between **Dominic Smith** and **Coby Mayo**. While **Coby Mayo** (46.80) possesses raw power, his score was suppressed by a lower projected spot in the batting order and a difficult matchup against Trey Yesavage. **Dominic Smith** (55.14) earned the nod as the final outfielder due to his superior platoon utility and better projected SP matchup against Brady Singer. Conversely, **Sam Antonacci** was relegated to the bench with a 36.44 score; despite a solid xwOBA, his matchup against Framber Valdez resulted in a platoon-heavy penalty that pushed him well below our 40-point efficiency floor. \n\nInvestors should remain cautious as every player in the starting nine\u2014including **Liam Hicks**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**\u2014is currently operating under a \"Lineup Pending\" designation. Risks are specifically concentrated in the lower half of the lineup: **Andy Pages** faces a significant headwind from Jes\u00fas Luzardo\u2019s elite hold capability, and **Nasim Nunez** suffers from a late-order penalty that caps his upside despite his speed-heavy profile. We are monitoring the **Jacob Wilson** injury status closely as he remains sidelined on the IL, but the depth of the current active roster provides sufficient coverage for today\u2019s 5x5 slate.",
